d/choices ["q-337533/field-2/a6d6f04c38773765f1bb82ede15adfeaf71459e9c969a5ee0dbe47144d615e1b" "q-337533/field-2/0de676b88d04b5b443737b0936f8cc9731b6457a079dd099505520764faf9e05" "q-337533/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-337533/field-2/b306ad6a3af7dc043f4c3e03da26a15440a9e9b19389783b2e1203bad6e37573" "q-337533/field-2/0548e424ed46c8ac5724289ef3709e4415ab7eab5e8e1a69e67e8d965f036008" "q-337533/field-2/c2b550d16a9f82ff5840df0aee64589283e87dadbb4156116e1615d2bde6ce7f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337533/field-3/0548e424ed46c8ac5724289ef3709e4415ab7eab5e8e1a69e67e8d965f036008" :answer/id #uuid "3477f2d9-8b83-59c5-94c2-ef9cab50edb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{6x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337533/field-3/a6d6f04c38773765f1bb82ede15adfeaf71459e9c969a5ee0dbe47144d615e1b" :answer/id #uuid "a2f9ca7a-6ce4-5928-a0ca-aea74f923bb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x{e}^{-6x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337533/field-3/c2b550d16a9f82ff5840df0aee64589283e87dadbb4156116e1615d2bde6ce7f" :answer/id #uuid "e3444fad-a327-55d0-bf94-492195ca781f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x{e}^{6x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337533/field-3/0de676b88d04b5b443737b0936f8cc9731b6457a079dd099505520764faf9e05" :answer/id #uuid "68755ee1-9167-51c8-a3c1-da85854f9d77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-6x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337533/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5e31c6b-2156-5254-9244-78abe674b418" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-337533/field-3/c2b550d16a9f82ff5840df0aee64589283e87dadbb4156116e1615d2bde6ce7f" :answer-field/choices ["q-337533/field-3/0548e424ed46c8ac5724289ef3709e4415ab7eab5e8e1a69e67e8d965f036008" "q-337533/field-3/a6d6f04c38773765f1bb82ede15adfeaf71459e9c969a5ee0dbe47144d615e1b" "q-337533/field-3/c2b550d16a9f82ff5840df0aee64589283e87dadbb4156116e1615d2bde6ce7f" "q-337533/field-3/0de676b88d04b5b443737b0936f8cc9731b6457a079dd099505520764faf9e05"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337533" :question/id #uuid "3500ae78-1cc6-5c2f-9a74-6462d1a0b3b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-337533" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-6y={e}^{6x}.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-6{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{6x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{6x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{6x})}^{′}-6(u{e}^{6x}) & ={e}^{6x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{6x}+6u{e}^{6x}-6u{e}^{6x} & ={e}^{6x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{6x}+\\cancel{6u{e}^{6x}}-\\cancel{6u{e}^{6x}} & ={e}^{6x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{6x} & ={e}^{6x} \\\\ {u}^{′} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =1 \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{6x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{6x} \\\\  & =x{e}^{6x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337533/field-1" "q-337533/field-2" "q-337533/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5fb547a-2518-5db9-b1b1-aab8d80328af"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337533"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338129/field-1/e98b833f0d251b374798371789a5f1a6437300a22cb039beb746d4ba9477adba" :answer/id #uuid "61e78fa5-9bad-5b54-b1fc-09cae2231558" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{9x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338129/field-1/80dedcd716cbf4bfcbb881a6b9e04d28115146cffc40f13409d93b7510c747c9" :answer/id #uuid "604c778f-b671-507e-a9d8-b3d0ac50bd1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{6x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338129/field-1/1be23322a705239834ee3034ce66e7e2d3abe104c3198062f03111fa44fff1d8" :answer/id #uuid "67d3c8b4-ce61-543e-bd7e-390f22c306ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338129/field-1/90244fea567263d29a122e974f426c797e64ce018b292ff9ad249e079209d91d" :answer/id #uuid "9f3bc0e0-9b9f-5538-a731-166ad58fae0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338129/field-1/104b19ddfff8532674993f9f432695275c1081fdb892f9b6b1664b5a8361b9ca" :answer/id #uuid "27d9c1bf-df94-5034-b7d5-c2fbdfa02570" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-6x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338129/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "723d8a84-678e-5285-a684-be8ef3d5591a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/cor