/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352892/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ff1666d-8206-58c7-8ac5-da234dc132b4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-352892/field-2/2975da8a53c33ab8dd27a0cb72f33922e3b3fc193461a85e5c75fe6369b275ef" :answer-field/choices ["q-352892/field-2/2975da8a53c33ab8dd27a0cb72f33922e3b3fc193461a85e5c75fe6369b275ef" "q-352892/field-2/7d6b9d97d4650230e0757b589dbaef1b0b8528126e1b69809d0e7949b2412c18" "q-352892/field-2/fc7dee5eb561f3402374f66f7b209aec00f6cc6148d0ca8add6a8f419af3c793" "q-352892/field-2/453ae6425bae6aab8ae02feb54871fdbfe7424196dcc465f60fbc3a42959262c" "q-352892/field-2/22b340f4b084760c64486987c1f227114a768c998b9f44d9bb4404dfa10ab38f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352892/field-3/32cb3076804c9419a7a298ef1016adb39bcc2c95952b7351afde08981aeab409" :answer/id #uuid "f7ceeae0-c237-5a45-bdd1-a02af30abc38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{9x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352892/field-3/874f7f58d76573226652a58d96e6555b5165a1fc6f405028c91744e8ee3dba39" :answer/id #uuid "9c17370a-28ae-503e-8962-d80b555d81ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352892/field-3/279df3b2e17888f6daef97328f388399ca903e7819c5d525760d1e68b4e82f6c" :answer/id #uuid "038a9f85-7961-5df4-ba32-d00e2a387840" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352892/field-3/7e9ef867b0851671fccc6e8a97e1b34733b8ded407bb3ea46b4bb715248dfddb" :answer/id #uuid "6ce223a7-b6f4-5df0-898a-5ccae4556d60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352892/field-3/4fcc48c0536364676dd8f7c2daec05b325a26dd1ea9e37917cc7cd555d652dd7" :answer/id #uuid "8b0a8034-0050-5ad8-9e55-735371a45d6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352892/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "d1f65fd1-cf0a-5578-b6d0-c23d9faa2fa1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-352892/field-3/7e9ef867b0851671fccc6e8a97e1b34733b8ded407bb3ea46b4bb715248dfddb" :answer-field/choices ["q-352892/field-3/32cb3076804c9419a7a298ef1016adb39bcc2c95952b7351afde08981aeab409" "q-352892/field-3/874f7f58d76573226652a58d96e6555b5165a1fc6f405028c91744e8ee3dba39" "q-352892/field-3/279df3b2e17888f6daef97328f388399ca903e7819c5d525760d1e68b4e82f6c" "q-352892/field-3/7e9ef867b0851671fccc6e8a97e1b34733b8ded407bb3ea46b4bb715248dfddb" "q-352892/field-3/4fcc48c0536364676dd8f7c2daec05b325a26dd1ea9e37917cc7cd555d652dd7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352892" :question/id #uuid "3b0212f2-f2fb-5e50-b8a7-448c254b9133" :question/math-academy-id "q-352892" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5y=2{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+5{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-5x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-5x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{-5x})}^{′}+5(u{e}^{-5x}) & =2{e}^{-x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-5x}-5u{e}^{-5x}+5u{e}^{-5x} & =2{e}^{-x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-5x}-\\cancel{5u{e}^{-5x}}+\\cancel{5u{e}^{-5x}} & =2{e}^{-x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-5x} & =2{e}^{-x} \\\\ {u}^{′} & =2{e}^{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =2{e}^{4x} \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{-5x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{-5x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4x}\\cdot {e}^{-5x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-352892/field-1" "q-352892/field-2" "q-352892/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ac34a18-053d-5eab-8c2c-bd0f15658186"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352892"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
